The brief has changed. Here is the change, in addition to everything the brief said before:

# Change 2: time out a task

The run can now give up on a task whose worker takes too long.

- `taskTimeout(task)`: for task 0 or 1, while the run is running or cancelling and the task is still assigned, the run records the task as **failed**, as if its worker had reported `failed` for the last time (it is not retried), and sends the worker `Abort`. Refused otherwise.
- A report that arrives later for a task that is no longer assigned is ignored.

Everything else is as before.

The host interface is now as follows, and `host.ts` has been updated to match.

```ts
// T7 after change 2, a run and its workers with task timeouts: the host interface every arm implements (PT13, S91).

/** A message sent by one part of the system to another, not yet delivered. */
export interface Message {
  id: string;
  from: string;
  to: string;
  action: string;
  data: Record<string, unknown>;
}

/** The network: nothing is delivered until deliver or deliverAll is called. */
export interface Network {
  /** Every message in transit, in no promised order. */
  inFlight(): Promise<Message[]>;
  /** Deliver one message in transit, by its id. */
  deliver(id: string): Promise<void>;
  /** Deliver every message in transit, and every message those deliveries send, until none is left. */
  deliverAll(): Promise<void>;
}

/** The outcome of a command: it took effect, or it was refused and changed nothing. */
export type Outcome = { ok: true } | { ok: false; reason: string };

export type TaskStatus = 'idle' | 'assigned' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'cancelled';

export interface RunView {
  status: 'idle' | 'running' | 'cancelling' | 'completed' | 'failed' | 'cancelled';
  task0: TaskStatus;
  task1: TaskStatus;
  retried0: boolean;
  retried1: boolean;
}

export interface Host extends Network {
  start(): Promise<Outcome>;
  workDone(worker: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  workFailed(worker: string): Promise<Outcome>;
  cancel(): Promise<Outcome>;
  taskTimeout(task: number): Promise<Outcome>;
  run(): Promise<RunView>;
  /** The worker "worker0" or "worker1", or null for any other id. */
  worker(worker: string): Promise<{ status: 'idle' | 'busy' } | null>;
}

/** The module's default export: a factory of a fresh system, with the run and its two workers. */
export type CreateHost = () => Promise<Host>;
```

Update your delivery to satisfy the brief as changed, keeping everything the change does not touch. Test your work as you go. When you are done, say so in one line.

